		    <br>
		    Biography on Ammer Outcaster:<br>
<br>
<br>
	Abandon by his own, Ammer was born without any knowledge of the world around him. Sent to Qeynos with nothing. No mother, no father, no friends...not even a god. Ammer was a lonely soul until level 8 where he was recruited into a guild called Bruin's Marauders. Led by<br>
Bruin, Ammer would come to know this world as evil and lonely. Yet, Ammer strived to find the reason why he was brought about. <br>
<br>
Later on, Ammer was disbanded by Bruin's Marauders for seeking out information that would harm the guild and Bruin. <br>
<br>
	After a long time Ammer joined the Misfits of Carnage led by the ex-officers of Bruin's Marauders, led by Dadio Daman/ Slashinbashn Bonebreaker. Raised by the family and friends of Misfits. After proving his loyalty to his guild he received officership and became an important icon to the Misfits. When times changed, Ammer felt it was time to move on to find what purpose he served in this world.<br>
<br>
	Ammer would come and go from guilds, trying to find happiness. No where could he find it. But, one day he met a girl named Mnemonique who quickly stole his heart at first sight. He was determined to meet her as soon as he could. Mnemonique brought all the happiness Ammer could want in his world. But, without the knowledge for why he belongs here... he seeks out more information.<br>
<br>
Though Ammer seeks knowledge he's a very fun loving guy. He likes to joke around and have fun however he can. But, when the time comes he can be as serious as a heart attack.<br>
	<br>
	As time goes on Ammer begins to understand more about the world around him. Being much more familiar of his surroundings. He also begins to seek some what of a reason why he thinks he's in this world. Wizards hold the ultimate power that no other soul on Norrath could. As a true Wizard Ammer developed into the Wizard he is now. Striving at the 46th season he gains experience in one day hoping to find the answer to his question. As his power becomes more and more divine Ammer begins to realize that the power he holds, many others seek him for help. Help as in destroying the evil that lurks on Norrath.<br>
<br>
	While Ammer strives to help others but, yet serve his role as Wizard. He has yet to find the true meaning of life and answer to his mind boggling question. Why?<br>
